1
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:51,000
In the grim darkness of the far future there is only war.

2
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Ultramarines: A Warhammer 40,000 Movie is a animation,
science fiction film directed by Martyn Pick.

3
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:21,000
A squad of Ultramarines answer a distress call from an Imperial Shrine World.

4
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
A full Company of Imperial Fists was stationed
there, but there is no answer from them.

5
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:51,000
The squad investigates to find out what has happened there.

6
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Severus (voice), played by Terence Stamp.

7
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Carnak, played by John Hurt.

8
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Proteus (voice), played by Sean Pertwee.

9
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:51,000
Verenor (voice), played by Steven Waddington.

10
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Pythol (voice), played by Donald Sumpter.

11
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:21,000
Nidon (voice), played by Johnny Harris.

12
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Ultramarines: A Warhammer 40,000 Movie is a 2010 British adult animated action science fiction film set in Games
Workshop's fictional Warhammer 40,000 universe and based on the Ultramarines Chapter of the Space Marines.

13
01:01:45,000 --> 01:01:51,000
Terence Stamp, Sean Pertwee, and John Hurt head the cast of voice actors, and
the screenplay was written by Black Library author Dan Abnett.

14
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
The film explores themes of space marine, demon,
adult animation, soldiers, warhammer.

15
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
